+# Performance history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+The read-path change moved `PRAGMA quick_check` to a recorded result, replaced the
+live FTS row count with the trigger-maintained `meta.fts_rows` counter, and relied
+on the `record.body` `CHECK (length(body) <= 2000)` constraint instead of rescanning
+record bodies. These changes landed together, so this history does not attribute
+the improvement to any one of them.
+
+| Version | 5k-record `SessionStart` p50 |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Before the read-path change | No measured p50 was found in this checkout or its available session records. |
+| After the read-path change | **1.006 ms** |
+
+The after measurement was taken on 2026-09-14 with the repository benchmark,
+using 5,000 records, 15,000 cues, and 300 end-to-end hook invocations:
+
+```text
+muninn-bench perf --records 5000 --cues 15000 --runs 300
+SessionStart: p50 1.005872 ms, p95 1.252231 ms, p99 1.348652 ms
+```
+
+The source notes a separate measured `quick_check` cost of 9.6 ms at a 5 MB
+database, but that is not a measured end-to-end `SessionStart` p50 and therefore
+is not used as the missing before value.
